WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.083
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.383 --> 00:00:08.770
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:15.251
Unit eighteen: Cultural Traditions. Today you will describe traditions with the passive voice.

4
00:00:15.551 --> 00:00:18.169
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:22.517
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.383 --> 00:00:24.199
Tradition.

7
00:00:25.183 --> 00:00:28.112
Tradition means a custom passed down over many years.

8
00:00:28.717 --> 00:00:30.937
Khmer New Year is an important tradition.

9
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.645
Your turn. Say: Tradition.

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.373
Tradition.

11
00:00:38.117 --> 00:00:38.967
Custom.

12
00:00:39.983 --> 00:00:42.993
Custom means a usual way of doing something in a culture.

13
00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:45.757
Bowing to elders is a Khmer custom.

14
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.956
Your turn. Say: Custom.

15
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:52.673
Custom.

16
00:00:53.417 --> 00:00:54.360
Heritage.

17
00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.569
Heritage means the culture and history passed to you.

18
00:00:59.183 --> 00:01:01.206
Angkor Wat is part of our heritage.

19
00:01:01.817 --> 00:01:04.481
Your turn. Say: Heritage.

20
00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.404
Heritage.

21
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.174
Ceremony.

22
00:01:11.183 --> 00:01:14.414
Ceremony means a formal event with special actions.

23
00:01:15.017 --> 00:01:17.248
The wedding ceremony lasted two days.

24
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.166
Your turn. Say: Ceremony.

25
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.164
Ceremony.

26
00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:25.953
Generation.

27
00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:30.285
Generation means all the people born around the same time.

28
00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:33.196
Three generations live in our house.

29
00:01:33.783 --> 00:01:36.169
Your turn. Say: Generation.

30
00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:40.081
Generation.

31
00:01:40.817 --> 00:01:41.864
Pass down.

32
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.511
Pass down means to give something to younger people.

33
00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:48.476
Recipes are passed down in my family.

34
00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:51.712
Your turn. Say: Pass down.

35
00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:55.637
Pass down.

36
00:01:56.383 --> 00:01:57.350
Ancestor.

37
00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.499
Ancestor means a family member who lived long ago.

38
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:04.512
We honour our ancestors at Pchum Ben.

39
00:02:05.117 --> 00:02:07.757
Your turn. Say: Ancestor.

40
00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.624
Ancestor.

41
00:02:12.383 --> 00:02:13.384
Preserve.

42
00:02:14.383 --> 00:02:16.975
Preserve means to keep something safe and alive.

43
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:19.606
We must preserve our traditions.

44
00:02:20.217 --> 00:02:22.741
Your turn. Say: Preserve.

45
00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:26.520
Preserve.

46
00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:30.938
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.783 --> 00:02:34.340
Visal, what tradition does your family follow?

48
00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.378
We follow the Pchum Ben ceremony every year.

49
00:02:39.483 --> 00:02:40.960
How is it celebrated?

50
00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:46.105
Food is offered to monks, and prayers are said for our ancestors.

51
00:02:47.217 --> 00:02:48.148
Who taught you?

52
00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:54.468
My grandmother. This ceremony is passed down through generations.

53
00:02:55.633 --> 00:02:57.018
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:57.883 --> 00:03:01.311
Grammar focus: Passive voice for traditions.

55
00:03:01.611 --> 00:03:02.925
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:03.617 --> 00:03:06.313
This ceremony is passed down through generations.

57
00:03:07.217 --> 00:03:08.914
Food is offered to monks.

58
00:03:09.817 --> 00:03:12.339
Traditional dances are performed at weddings.

59
00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:19.955
In the passive, the object of the action becomes the subject: Someone passes it down → It is passed down.

60
00:03:20.717 --> 00:03:25.412
Be careful! Don't say: This ceremony passed down through generations.

61
00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:30.841
Say: This ceremony is passed down through generations.

62
00:03:31.141 --> 00:03:32.943
The passive needs 'is' or 'are'.

63
00:03:33.733 --> 00:03:36.258
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:38.439
Keeping Culture Alive.

65
00:03:38.739 --> 00:03:41.935
Cultural traditions and customs connect us to our heritage.

66
00:03:42.933 --> 00:03:46.419
Many ceremonies are passed down from one generation to the next.

67
00:03:47.433 --> 00:03:51.140
At Pchum Ben, food is offered to monks to honour our ancestors.

68
00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:54.551
Traditional songs are taught to children at home.

69
00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:58.530
Preserving these traditions keeps our culture alive.

70
00:03:59.633 --> 00:04:03.600
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.531
This ceremony blank passed down.

72
00:04:06.831 --> 00:04:09.881
A, is. B, are. C, be.

73
00:04:13.433 --> 00:04:15.143
The answer is A: is.

74
00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:19.618
A family member who lived long ago is an blank.

75
00:04:19.918 --> 00:04:23.908
A, ancestor. B, generation. C, heritage.

76
00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:29.722
The answer is A: ancestor.

77
00:04:30.883 --> 00:04:33.324
To keep something safe and alive is to blank.

78
00:04:33.624 --> 00:04:37.742
A, preserve. B, pass down. C, celebrate.

79
00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.358
The answer is A: preserve.

80
00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:47.579
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:48.417 --> 00:04:50.637
What is a tradition your family follows?

82
00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:00.846
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:01.146 --> 00:05:08.825
My family follows the Khmer New Year tradition. Water is poured on our grandparents' hands, and we ask for their blessing.

84
00:05:09.125 --> 00:05:10.753
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:16.740
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive voice for traditions.

86
00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:22.061
Today's value is cultural pride. Be proud of Khmer festivals and traditions.

87
00:05:22.361 --> 00:05:25.060
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

88
00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:28.755
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

